QUESTION NO: 6

A = {1, 2, 3, 4}
B = {3, 4, 5, 6}

# All unique elements
print("Union:", A | B)

# Common elemnts
print("Intersection:", A & B)

# Difference
print("A - B:", A - B)
print("B - A:", B - A)

# In either A or B but not both
print("Symmetric difference:" A ^ B)

Why A - B and B - A differ:
Answer: A - B keeps the elemnts that are only in A(1,2), while B - A
keeps the elemnts that are ony in B(5,6). The order matters,so the results are differnet.
